{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the final interpretation for the joint-apply investigation with the receipt behind it (CheckRun f80378ddde474d69956d0df5d2e1a141 indices 63-64 and 115): at seed 35 the same node appended both changes, the second with applied=3, pendingConfIndex=2 and a non-joint tracker although its own log already contained the joint change at index 2 - a tracker state in-order application cannot produce and the harness's restart path can, since it rebuilds a node with Config.Applied from its applied index while restoring the tracker from a ConfState written from the tracker rather than from the log that index covers. The interpretation therefore stays explained with the defect claim refuted, and the residue relevant to the target is the documented robustness boundary: the propose-time check is best-effort against leader-local state and an invalid change reaching apply is process-fatal, which matters to a caller who disables that check or restores state whose tracker does not match its log. I also attempted to close the two remaining gaps (the sweep's measurement question and the proposer-state question) and the controller rejected those attempts with 'answer only gaps belonging to this experiment lineage, or give a source-only correction' - both gaps were registered against earlier experiments in their investigations while the receipts that answer them belong to the newer append-instrumented experiment, so the closure has to be submitted under the right lineage or as a source-only account, which the next turn can do. State of the run: four investigations carry terminal accounts (campaign admission explained/refuted, ReadIndex loss across a term change explained/refuted, transfer delayed-but-bounded holds/refuted, joint-change ordering explained/refuted after one turn at asserted), the sweep investigation holds with two open gaps (its measurement question now answerable by the applicability counter, and the coverage items), and no experiment is outstanding; the declared allocation still shows room, so the next action is to re-record the two gap answers under the correct lineage.\"}"}}
